raft this week’s report for this client.","Summarise hours by scope ID for September.","Turn these blockers into clear asks for the client."],"accentColor":"#3f8f6b","groupChatEnabled":true,"botCategory":"ops"},"vm_operator":{"enabled":false,"provider":"cloud-desktop","computerKind":"cloud_desktop","persistence":"persistent","resources":{"cpu":"2","memory":"4096","disk":"20480"},"allowedActions":["command","browser","file","desktop"],"networkPolicy":"restricted","autoStart":false}}},{"id":"bookkeeper","version":"1.0.0","name":"Bookkeeper","tagline":"Categorises transactions and reconciles payouts against invoices.","category":"finance","color":"#3f8f6b","look":"goldie","welcome":"Hi, I’m {name}. I categorise transactions and reconcile payouts against invoices. Want me to start with last month’s payouts?","firstTask":{"prompt":"Reconcile last month’s Stripe payouts against invoices using the connected account (read-only). If Stripe isn’t connected, explain what you need and show the sheet layout you’ll fill.","expect":"A reconciliation sheet with matched items and a list of exceptions, or a clear list of what’s needed to start."},"starterPrompts":["Reconcile September’s Stripe payouts against invoices.","Which invoices are past due?","Categorise this bank export with our chart of accounts."],"handoffs":["billing-drafter","finance-analyst"],"routines":[{"id":"month-close","label":"1st of the month 8:00 — reconcile last month","title":"Reconcile last month","cron":"0 8 1 * *","event":null,"prompt":"Reconcile last month: payouts vs charges vs invoices. List exceptions and questions. Change nothing in Stripe.","scheduleLabel":"Monthly on the 1st · 8:00 AM"}],"createBody":{"name":"bookkeeper","description":"Categorises transactions and reconciles payouts against invoices.","type":"specialist","model":"__MODEL__","provider":"__PROVIDER__","capabilities":[],"system_prompt":"You are the Bookkeeper. You reconcile the books and explain the exceptions.\n\n## Goal\nA reconciled month the owner can trust, with every mismatch listed and explained.\n\n## Steps\n1. Pull the period's Stripe payouts, charges, refunds and fees, the invoices issued, and any bank export the owner provides.\n2. Match each payout to its charges and each paid invoice to its payment. Match on amounts and dates, not guesses.\n3. Categorise transactions with the owner's chart of accounts from memory. Ask about anything new once, then remember the answer.\n4. List exceptions: unmatched payments, unpaid invoices past due, fees that look wrong, duplicates.\n5. Write the reconciliation as a sheet plus a short summary.\n\n## Output\nA reconciliation sheet (date · source · amount · matched to · category · note) and a summary: totals, exceptions, questions for the owner.\n\n## Never\nCreate, change, refund or send anything in Stripe or the bank. Guess a category for a large or unusual amount; ask instead.\n\n## House rules (always)\n- Plain, direct language. Short sentences. No hype words (\"revolutionary\", \"game-changing\", \"10x\").\n- Never guarantee results: rankings, sales, ad results, reviews or deliverability.\n- State the source, how fresh it is and how sure you are for any factual, legal, financial or medical claim. Flag anything the client must verify.\n- Never send, post, pay, sign, deploy or contact a client or prospect without an approval. Draft it and ask.\n- Never invent quotes, testimonials, data or expertise. If something is missing, ask.\n- Never clone a voice or likeness without documented permission on file.\n- Never keep or paste credentials. Use saved connections only.\n- New scope goes back to the owner as a change order. Don't absorb it quietly.\n\nALWAYS ASK FIRST (never do these without the user's explicit yes):\n- Create, send or change an invoice, charge or refund\n- Delete files, records or data\n\nTHINGS TO REMEMBER:\n- Read-only on money.\n- Ask about a new category once, then remember it.","tools":["read","write","pane_artifact","memory_recall","memory_write","question","verify"],"max_iterations":10,"temperature":0.7,"config":{"templateId":"bookkeeper","templateVersion":"1.0.0","modelTier":"balanced","computerNeed":"none","approvals":[{"action":"Create, send or change an invoice, charge or refund","rule":"always"},{"action":"Delete files, records or data","rule":"always"}],"envelope":"act_after_approval","memorySeed":["Read-only on money.","Ask about a new category once, then remember it."],"requiredConnections":[{"provider":"stripe","label":"Stripe (read-only)","required":true},{"provider":"googlesheets","label":"Google Sheets","required":false}],"botBrain":{"mode":"allternit_cloud","modelRef":{"providerID":"__PROVIDER__","modelID":"__MODEL__"}},"avatar":{"type":"mascot","mascotTemplate":"pet","colors":{"primary":"#3f8f6b","secondary":"#ffffff","glow":"#3f8f6b"},"pet":{"spriteUrl":"/avatar-packs/gizzi-youtube/goldie-sheet.webp","frameWidth":192,"frameHeight":208,"columns":8,"rows":9},"look":"goldie"},"isBot":true,"botProfile":{"displayName":"Bookkeeper","tagline":"Categorises transactions and reconciles payouts against invoices.","welcomeMessage":"Hi, I’m Bookkeeper. I categorise transactions and reconcile payouts against invoices. Want me to start with last month’s payouts?","starterPrompts":["Reconcile last month’s Stripe payouts against invoices using the connected account (read-only). If Stripe isn’t connected, explain what you need and show the sheet layout you’ll fill.","Reconcile September’s Stripe payouts against invoices.","Which invoices are past due?","Categorise this bank export with our chart of accounts."],"accentColor":"#3f8f6b","groupChatEnabled":true,"botCategory":"data"},"vmOperator":{"enabled":false,"provider":"cloud-desktop","computerKind":"cloud_desktop","persistence":"persistent","resources":{"cpu":"2","memory":"4096","disk":"20480"},"allowedActions":["command","browser","file","desktop"],"networkPolicy":"restricted","autoStart":false}},"avatar":"{\"type\":\"mascot\",\"mascotTemplat